WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.920
The OWASP Top 10 provides a practical recap of common application risks:

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.860
broken access control, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.520
misconfiguration, vulnerable components, authentication failures, integrity failures,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.620
logging failures, and SSRF.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:24.360
CMMC practice domains help translate those risks into expectations for access control,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.300
audit and accountability, configuration management, identification and authentication,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.480
risk assessment, security assessment, system protection, and system integrity.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:40.300
Protecting CUI requires shared responsibility across software developers, DevSecOps teams,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.480
security engineers, IT administrators, defense contractors, compliance teams,

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.940
and technical managers. Completion of this training is awareness-level only.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.840
It does not constitute certification, assessment completion,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.460
or proof of full organizational compliance.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.640
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, CMMC practice references,

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:07.300
secure coding checklists, a glossary, an OWASP-to-CMMC mapping matrix,

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.360
developer quick-reference sheets, and audit support documentation.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.460
Use this course as an awareness and planning aid.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.600
Validate practice applicability against the organization's CMMC scope.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.060
Maintain evidence for secure development, monitoring, configuration,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.200
and remediation activities.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:33.820
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include CA.L2-3.12.1 - Security assessments;

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:43.160
RA.L2-3.11.1 - Risk assessments; SI.L2-3.14.2 - Flaw remediation.
